\p \v 7 \w In the twelfth|strong="H08147"\w* \w year|strong="H08141"\w* \w of King|strong="H04428"\w* \w Xerxes|strong="H00325"\w*, \w in the first|strong="H07223"\w* \w month|strong="H02320"\w*, \w the month|strong="H02320"\w* \w of Nisan|strong="H05212"\w*,\f + \fr 3:7 \fqa Nisan \ft is the first month of the Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of March and April.\f* \w the Pur|strong="H06332"\w* \w (that is|strong="H01931"\w*, \w the lot|strong="H01486"\w*) \w was cast|strong="H05307"\w* \w before|strong="H06440"\w* \w Haman|strong="H02001"\w* \w to determine a day|strong="H03117"\w* \w and month|strong="H02320"\w*. \w And the lot fell on the twelfth|strong="H08147"\w* \w month|strong="H02320"\w*, \w the month of Adar|strong="H00143"\w*.\f + \fr 3:7 \ft LXX \fqa was cast before Haman—a day and month—and the lot fell on the fourteenth of the month of Adar\ft ; Hebrew \fqa was cast before Haman a day and month—the twelfth, Adar\ft ; the month of \fqa Adar \ft (also in verse 13) is the twelfth month of the Hebrew lunar calendar, usually occurring within the months of February and March.\f*
\p \v 8 \w Then Haman|strong="H02001"\w* \w informed|strong="H00559"\w* \w King|strong="H04428"\w* \w Xerxes|strong="H00325"\w*, “\w There|strong="H03426"\w* \w is a certain|strong="H00259"\w* \w people|strong="H05971"\w* \w scattered|strong="H06340"\w* \w and dispersed|strong="H06504"\w* \w among|strong="H00996"\w* \w the peoples|strong="H05971"\w* \w of every|strong="H03605"\w* \w province|strong="H04082"\w* \w of your kingdom|strong="H04438"\w*. \w Their laws|strong="H01881"\w* \w are different|strong="H08138"\w* \w from everyone|strong="H03605"\w* \w else’s|strong="H05971"\w*, \w and they do not|strong="H00369"\w* \w obey|strong="H06213"\w* \w the king’s|strong="H04428"\w* \w laws|strong="H01881"\w*. \w So it is not|strong="H00369"\w* \w in the king’s|strong="H04428"\w* \w best interest|strong="H07737"\w* \w to tolerate them|strong="H05117"\w*. \v 9 \w If|strong="H00518"\w* \w it pleases|strong="H02896"\w* \w the king|strong="H04428"\w*, \w let a decree be issued|strong="H03789"\w* \w to destroy them|strong="H00006"\w*, \w and I will deposit|strong="H00935"\w* \w ten|strong="H06235"\w* \w thousand|strong="H00505"\w* \w talents|strong="H03603"\w* \w of silver|strong="H03701"\w*\f + \fr 3:9 \fqa 10,000 talents \ft is approximately 377 tons or 342 metric tons of silver.\f* \w into|strong="H00413"\w* \w the royal|strong="H04428"\w* \w treasury|strong="H01595"\w* \w to pay|strong="H08254"\w* \w those who carry it out|strong="H06213"\w*.”
