\c 6
\s1 Mordecai Is Honored
\p \v 1 \w That|strong="H01931"\w* \w night|strong="H03915"\w* \w sleep|strong="H08142"\w* \w escaped|strong="H05074"\w* \w the king|strong="H04428"\w*; \w so he ordered|strong="H00559"\w* \w the Book|strong="H05612"\w* \w of Records|strong="H02146"\w*, \w the Chronicles|strong="H01697"\w*,\f + \fr 6:1 \ft Or \fqa the Book of Memorials, the Annals \ft or \fqa the Book of Records of Historical Events\f* \w to be|strong="H01961"\w* \w brought in|strong="H00935"\w* \w and read|strong="H07121"\w* \w to|strong="H06440"\w* \w him|strong="H04428"\w*. \v 2 \w And there it was found|strong="H04672"\w* \w recorded|strong="H03789"\w* \w that|strong="H00834"\w* \w Mordecai|strong="H04782"\w* \w had exposed|strong="H05046"\w* \w Bigthana|strong="H00904"\w*\f + \fr 6:2 \fqa Bigthana \ft is a variant of \fqa Bigthan\ft ; see Esther 2:21.\f* \w and Teresh|strong="H08657"\w*, \w two|strong="H08147"\w* \w of the eunuchs|strong="H05631"\w* \w who guarded|strong="H08104"\w* \w the king’s|strong="H04428"\w* \w entrance|strong="H05592"\w*, \w when|strong="H00834"\w* \w they had conspired|strong="H01245"\w* \w to assassinate|strong="H07971"\w* \w King|strong="H04428"\w* \w Xerxes|strong="H00325"\w*.
